I settled #1036 by choosing to refuse. If the config file yoyo loads has an unterminated quote or a [section header with no closing ], starting a session now stops with one error and exit code 2, before any API call. That covers the REPL, -p, piped input and yoyo review. The error names each file:line and the problem, and says how to get going: fix the line, or move the file aside. Build, all tests, clippy, fmt check and tests/harness_logic.sh pass, and it's committed as e25b3cf2.

Why refuse: nobody writes an unterminated quote on purpose, so the old quiet default wasn't protecting anyone who chose it. Everyone who hit it had made a typo they didn't know about, and yoyo sent the value with the stray quote anyway (a 404 for model) and still exited 0. I ran the tools users already know on the same broken files, and all three refuse:

| Tool | What it did | Exit |
|---|---|---|
| git config --file bad.cfg --get a.b | fatal: bad config line 2 | 128 |
| cargo metadata with name = "x | invalid basic string | 101 |
| python3 tomllib.load | TOMLDecodeError | 1 |

The checker had a false positive, now fixed. Before letting it block startup, I tested it against valid TOML shapes and this repo's own .yoyo.toml read from disk. One shape wrongly fired: lines inside a multi-line """ / ''' string were checked as if they were config, so a line like [x or k = "v in a prompt would have refused a valid file. The checker now skips the inside of multi-line strings. One existing near-miss test had a bare prompt = """ line in the middle of its list, which would now hide every line after it. I moved that line to the end so the test still checks the same lines; no assertion was removed.

Inspection commands still only warn, on purpose. yoyo config get, config show, doctor, model and permissions print the old warning and keep working. They never send anything to a provider, and they're how you look at the file the error points to. yoyo review does call a provider, so it refuses too.

What I checked:
• Test failure checks, run one at a time and undone afterwards (no sabotage left in the tree): breaking the checker makes refusal_names_file_line_problem_and_remedy fail by name. Removing the multi-line skip makes valid_toml_shapes_never_fire fail.
• Running the real binary on model = "claude-haiku-5-5 (no closing quote) gives the error and exit 2 for both -p and piped input, while config get warns and exits 0.
• With this repo's valid config, -p "Reply with exactly PONG" printed PONG and exited 0.

Changes outside the task's file list:
• src/config.rs: one call and its comment changed in the shared config loader.
• src/dispatch_sub.rs: one line so review refuses too.
• ARCHITECTURE.md: the config_syntax.rs entry, which still said "detection-only".

docs/src/troubleshooting/common-issues.md now describes the refusal, the exit code and the fix.

Known gaps:
• A multi-line string that is never closed makes the checker skip the rest of the file, so later problems there go unreported. That can let a bad file through, but it can never refuse a good one.
• The refusal only applies when the command's first word isn't one of yoyo's subcommands. If a listed subcommand ever falls through to a normal session, that session would only warn.
